{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792946208,"nonce":"IifFBVCZpcxGO/v2zW0KQqHKrNg=","title":"Clone a repository into a workspace","message":"There is no way to start from a repository: Welcome offers Open Project and New Project only. Add Clone Repository, on the desktop and in the browser.\n\n**Flow**\n\n- Entry points: Welcome, the File menu and the command center. Input: a URL (https or ssh) or `owner/repo` shorthand for GitHub, an optional branch or tag, and a destination folder (desktop) or the session's workspace (web).\n- Progress and cancel while it runs (objects received, bytes), then open the result: detect the project kind (hxml, haxelib, rayzor, cbproj, folder) and open it as Open Project does; offer to pick one when a repository holds several.\n- Errors a person can act on: not found or private, authentication needed or refused, destination exists and is not empty, no network, too large.\n\n**Desktop**\n\nThe git extension already carries libgit2 (natives built with system OpenSSH for ssh, scripts/build-libgit2.sh). Clone through it, with credentials from the SSH agent and the system's credential helper, never stored by RayDE. A shallow clone option for large repositories.\n\n**Web**\n\nThe session does the clone into its workspace; the page never holds a token.\n- Public GitHub repositories: fetch the archive for the ref (no history) as the fast path, so a playground opens in seconds; a full clone follows on request.\n- Full clone and private repositories: libgit2 wasm with a fetch transport (git-bug 18e2769), or git in a container where the session has one (670bd15).\n- Private repositories need a separate, explicit GitHub consent for read access on top of the sign-in that gates editing (52138fc); the token stays in the session, is scoped to the repository, and expires with it.\n- Limits from the abuse issue (080ea85): repository size, clone time, one clone at a time per identity.\n- A link opens a repository directly: `?repo=owner/name\u0026ref=main`, which is what the Rayzor playground needs for its examples.\n\n**Done when** a repository can be cloned from Welcome on the desktop and from a page against a session, opens as a project, and the checks cover a local bare repository as the remote, an existing destination, a bad URL and a cancelled clone.","files":null}]}